# The parent of the two Flyway migration locations. It deliberately holds NO migration script.
#
#   db/migration/schema  V1__create_schema.sql, V2__create_indexes.sql   - resolved by EVERY profile
#   db/migration/seed    V3__seed_reference_data.sql,                    - resolved by LOCAL and TEST
#                        V4__seed_user_security.sql                        only; production is refused it
#
# Why the split, and why nothing may sit here: a Flyway location is scanned RECURSIVELY, so a script
# placed in this parent is reached by any profile that lists the parent, and a profile that lists the
# parent reaches the seeds through the child directory. Keeping the parent empty of scripts is what
# makes the location list a real boundary, which is the mechanism the module plan specifies -
# FlywayConfig resolves V3 and V4 from profile-scoped locations so a production deployment migrates
# schema and indexes without inheriting sample data or seeded credentials.
#
# Production is additionally held below the seeds by spring.flyway.target=2, and a database that has
# already been seeded is refused outright by ProductionSeedRejectionCallback. Three controls, in that
# order of precedence. See docs/decision-log.md DL-127.
#
# Do not add a script to this directory, and do not rename a script: each file name is a load-bearing
# Flyway log token.
